EVIDENCE:

## Summary

The projection's logic is correct on every axis I could break EXCEPT the one
the brief singled out by name. Requirement 6 says in so many words: "a
shortfall of exactly 100 must not become 200." It does, for 24% of
cent-valued inputs, because `roundUpToHundred` is the only float comparison
in the file with no epsilon. The worker's boundary test passes only because
its fixture (800 - 400) happens to be float-exact.

FAIL on item 6. Items 1-5 and 7-10 pass, with four non-blocking notes.

